# Policy general content
page('payment-policy/index.html','Payment Policy','Three AM Web + IT payment policy.',hero(['<a href="../index.html">Home</a>','<span aria-current="page">Payment policy</span>'],'Information','Payment Policy','Information about invoices, project payments and late-payment terms.')+'''<section class="section"><div class="shell policy-copy"><p>Three AM Web &amp; IT will provide clients with itemised electronic and/or paper invoices that outline the request, terms, methods of payment and other details.</p><h2>Invoice terms</h2><p>Invoices carry a 14 day term of payment from the date of invoice unless expressed otherwise in writing. Payment can be made via direct bank transfer (preferred), credit card (via eWay) or cheque.</p><h2>Project payment schedule</h2><ul><li><strong>Commencement deposit:</strong> A deposit calculated at 30% of the total quoted project value plus GST is required prior to commencing work.</li><li><strong>Progress payments:</strong> May be requested at stages of completion or milestones, depending on scope, size and nature of the project.</li><li><strong>Closing payment:</strong> An invoice for the final sum is sent once quoted work has been completed.</li><li><strong>Variations:</strong> Variations are invoiced as progress payments and itemised to reflect the specific variation.</li></ul><p>Refer to the current policy in the live system before publishing, as payment methods and fees may change.</p></div></section>''')
